## Setup

Use Ruby 3.4.11 and Bundler 4.0.21. The Gemfile accepts Ruby 3.3 through 4.x. Puma compiles a native extension and needs your platform's compiler toolchain.

```sh
bundle install
bundle exec rake build
bundle exec rake test
bundle exec ruby bin/proof
bundle exec ruby bin/server
```

`build` checks every Ruby entry point's syntax. `test` runs Minitest through Rack::Test. `bin/proof` starts a real Puma process on an available loopback port, parses its JSON response, rejects an invalid request, and stops the process. Commit the generated Gemfile.lock after installation to pin transitive dependencies. No lockfile is fabricated by the generator.

## HTTP contract

- GET `/health` returns `{"status":"ok","service":"{{rubyWebFramework}}"}`.
- POST `/api/greetings` accepts exactly `{"name":"Ruby"}` and returns `{"greeting":"Hello, Ruby!"}`.
- Blank, non-string, unknown-field, and over-80-character names return 422. Malformed JSON returns 400, non-JSON content returns 415, and bodies over 16 KiB return 413.

The server binds to `127.0.0.1:{{rubyPort}}`. `HOST`, `PORT`, `RACK_ENV`, and `ALLOWED_ORIGIN` are process environment variables. `.env.example` documents values and is not loaded automatically. CORS permits the generated frontend origins `{{rubyWebOrigin}}` by default. Set ALLOWED_ORIGIN to a comma-separated list of trusted frontend origins to override them. Host authorization accepts localhost and loopback addresses. Configure explicit trusted hosts before public hosting.

`http_policy.rb` enforces the host and origin allowlists and answers CORS preflight requests for every framework. `request_body_limit.rb` caps request bodies before the framework reads them, and `name_input.rb` validates the JSON payload.{{#if (eq rubyWebFramework "rails")}} Rails runs in API-only mode from a single `app.rb` application; set `SECRET_KEY_BASE` when `RACK_ENV=production`.{{/if}}

Use Ctrl-C to stop the foreground server. Add future routes in `app.rb` and behavior tests in `test/app_test.rb`. Keep Gemfile ownership inside this service when composed with other languages.

This source recipe is experimental. Generation, build, and runtime claims require proof for the exact producer revision and toolchains.
